    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r = 6.37 \\times 10^6 + 2.00 \\times 10^6 = 8.37 \\times 10^6\\ \\text{m}\"></span> 1 mark</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"g = \\frac{GM}{r^2} = \\frac{6.67 \\times 10^{-11} \\cdot 5.97 \\times 10^{24}}{(8.37 \\times 10^6)^2} = 5.70\\ \\text{N kg}^{-1}\"></span><br/>Correct substitution 1 mark , correct final answer with unit 1 mark</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v = \\sqrt{gr} = \\sqrt{5.70 \\cdot 8.37 \\times 10^6} = 6920\\ \\text{m s}^{-1}\"></span><br/>Correct formula 1 mark , correct final answer 1 mark</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong></p><p>Gravitational field strength is inversely proportional to the square of the distance from the mass centre, so it weakens with altitude. 1 mark</p></section>"
