  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A satellite is in circular orbit <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.00 \\times 10^6\\ \\text{m}\"></span> above the surface of Earth. The radius of Earth is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.37 \\times 10^6\\ \\text{m}\"></span>, and Earth’s mass is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.97 \\times 10^{24}\\ \\text{kg}\"></span>.</p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Calculate the distance from the centre of the Earth to the satellite. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Determine the gravitational field strength at the satellite’s altitude. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> Calculate the orbital speed required for the satellite to stay in circular orbit. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> Explain why the gravitational field strength decreases with altitude. [1]</p></section>"
